+(duration-opts)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, like `120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit, like `1h30m`. The units are `d`
+(days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may be used at most once, and units must be given in
+that order. Units are case-insensitive, and spaces are not allowed.
+
+Valid values include `120`, `2d`, `1h30m`, `45S`, `1d2h3m4s`, and `90m`. Values such as `1.5h`, `-5m`, `30m1h`,
+`1h1h`, or `1h 30m` are rejected.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    println()
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    println()
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+    println()
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
